ity. Yet he learned to depend on God rather than himself.</p><p>Jesus is the perfect example of meekness. <strong>Matthew 11:29 (ESV)</strong> says, <strong>&ldquo;Take my yoke upon you, and learn from me, for I am gentle and lowly in heart.&rdquo;</strong> Jesus had all authority, power, and glory, yet He humbled Himself completely.</p><p>Meekness frees a person from the exhausting burden of constantly defending themselves. A meek person does not need to fight for status because their identity is secure in God. They do not need to control every outcome because they trust the Father's sovereignty.</p><p>True strength is not found in dominating others. True strength is found in remaining obedient to God when pride demands its own way.</p></div><div class="devotion-nav"><a class="btn outline small" href="/series/blessed-are.html">Back to Blessed Are</a><a class="btn primary small" href="/devotions.html">Read Daily Dose</a></div></article></div></main><script src="/script-brand-share-v6.js"></script><script src="/pwa.js?v=pwa-4"></script>  <script src="/analytics-consent.js?v=1"></script>
