-</head><body data-publish-at="2026-10-04T18:00:00Z"><nav class="navbar scrolled" id="navbar"><div class="nav-inner"><a class="brand" href="/index.html#home"><img class="brand-logo" src="/icons/brand-mark-v3.png" alt="" aria-hidden="true"><span>DAILY DOSE</span></a><div class="nav-links"><a href="/index.html#home">Home</a><a href="/story.html">About</a><a href="/devotions.html">Devotions</a><a href="/series.html">Series</a><a href="/verse-library.html">Verse Library</a><a href="/prayer">Prayer</a><a href="mailto:dailydosedevotions@gmail.com">Contact</a></div><button class="menu-btn" id="menuBtn">&#9776;</button></div></nav><main class="devotion-shell series-shell"><div class="container"><a class="back-link" href="/series/blessed-are.html">&larr; Back to Blessed Are</a><article class="devotion-article reveal visible"><p class="eyebrow">Daily Dose: Blessed Are</p><h1>Blessed Are: The Peacemakers - Part 7</h1><div class="devotion-meta">Releases Sunday Oct 4, 2026 at 7:00PM</div><div class="devotion-body formed-body"><div class="scripture-box"><h3>Matthew 5:9 (ESV)</h3><p><strong>&ldquo;Blessed are the peacemakers, for they shall be called sons of God.&rdquo;</strong></p></div><p>Almost everyone says they want peace, but not everyone knows how to pursue peace biblically. Biblical peace goes deeper than avoiding disagreement or keeping things quiet on the surface. Jesus is blessing those who make peace.</p><p>A peacemaker brings the character of God into places where bitterness, division, pride, anger, and brokenness try to rule. Biblical peacemaking requires both grace and truth.</p><p>Abigail's life in 1 Samuel 25 gives a beautiful example. David and Nabal were moving toward violent conflict, but Abigail stepped into the middle with courage, humility, wisdom, and honour. <strong>1 Samuel 25:32-33 (ESV)</strong> records David saying, <strong>&ldquo;Blessed be the LORD... who sent you this day to meet me!&rdquo;</strong> and <strong>&ldquo;Blessed be your discretion.&rdquo;</strong></p><p>Jesus Himself shows us perfect peacemaking. He never compromised truth to please people, but He also never created division through ego, selfishness, or uncontrolled emotion.</p><p><strong>Colossians 3:13-15 (ESV)</strong> says, <strong>&ldquo;forgiving each other; as the Lord has forgiven you,&rdquo;</strong> and <strong>&ldquo;let the peace of Christ rule in your hearts.&rdquo;</strong></p><p>Barnabas also reflected peacemaking when many believers were afraid of Paul after his conversion. <strong>Acts 9:27 (ESV)</strong> says, <strong>&ldquo;Barnabas took him and brought him to the apostles.&rdquo;</strong></p><p>At the centre of the gospel is peace with God through Jesus Christ. <strong>Romans 5:1 (ESV)</strong> says, <strong>&ldquo;we have peace with God through our Lord Jesus Christ.&rdquo;</strong></p></div><div class="devotion-nav"><a class="btn outline small" href="/series/blessed-are.html">Back to Blessed Are</a><a class="btn primary small" href="/devotions.html">Read Daily Dose</a></div></article></div></main><script src="/script-brand-share-v6.js"></script><script src="/pwa.js?v=pwa-4"></script></body></html>
