-</head><body data-publish-at="2026-10-11T18:00:00Z"><nav class="navbar scrolled" id="navbar"><div class="nav-inner"><a class="brand" href="/index.html#home"><img class="brand-logo" src="/icons/brand-mark-v3.png" alt="" aria-hidden="true"><span>DAILY DOSE</span></a><div class="nav-links"><a href="/index.html#home">Home</a><a href="/story.html">About</a><a href="/devotions.html">Devotions</a><a href="/series.html">Series</a><a href="/verse-library.html">Verse Library</a><a href="/prayer">Prayer</a><a href="mailto:dailydosedevotions@gmail.com">Contact</a></div><button class="menu-btn" id="menuBtn">&#9776;</button></div></nav><main class="devotion-shell series-shell"><div class="container"><a class="back-link" href="/series/blessed-are.html">&larr; Back to Blessed Are</a><article class="devotion-article reveal visible"><p class="eyebrow">Daily Dose: Blessed Are</p><h1>Blessed Are: Those Persecuted For Righteousness' Sake - Part 8</h1><div class="devotion-meta">Releases Sunday Oct 11, 2026 at 7:00PM</div><div class="devotion-body formed-body"><div class="scripture-box"><h3>Matthew 5:10 (ESV)</h3><p><strong>&ldquo;Blessed are those who are persecuted for righteousness' sake, for theirs is the kingdom of heaven.&rdquo;</strong></p></div><p>This is one of the hardest Beatitudes because it speaks about rejection, opposition, pain, and personal cost. Yet Jesus includes persecution in the life of the believer because true righteousness will eventually collide with a world that does not surrender to God.</p><p>Jesus is not speaking about suffering caused by arrogance, harshness, foolishness, pride, or needless conflict. He says they are persecuted for righteousness' sake. The blessing is attached to suffering because a person chooses obedience to God over approval from the world.</p><p>Stephen's life gives a powerful example. <strong>Acts 6:10 (ESV)</strong> says, <strong>&ldquo;they could not withstand the wisdom and the Spirit with which he was speaking.&rdquo;</strong> Even